00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:06.736
Use the chat to connect
with other attendees

00:03:10.971 --> 00:03:15.510
Julia Undeutsch: A few years ago, there
was a brief period of time when I was

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.979
working on a website using the Divi theme.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.554
I actually hardly ever work with
WordPress because I prefer coding on

00:03:22.554 --> 00:03:25.882
my own, especially when it's a small
website and it's all for myself.

00:03:26.169 --> 00:03:31.832
But that's when I noticed there was
a paid accessibility plugin by Divi.

00:03:32.888 --> 00:03:33.625
I was baffled.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.461
What's that all about, guys?

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:39.181
If you already know that your
theme lacks code quality, how dare

00:03:39.181 --> 00:03:42.614
you develop a plugin to fix your
own crappy code and make people

00:03:42.673 --> 00:03:44.147
pay twice for it on top of that?

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:46.595
Think about it.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:49.379
Seriously, let that sink in for a moment.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.101
I'm Julia.

00:03:52.783 --> 00:03:57.420
I am self-taught front-end developer
based in Vienna, and I fell in love with

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:03.532
coding during COVID, and specialized
myself on accessibility there very on.

00:04:04.142 --> 00:04:09.874
I know that accessibility is scary,
and nowadays, accessibility plugins

00:04:09.874 --> 00:04:14.034
are popping out everywhere saying,
"I can make your website accessible

00:04:14.039 --> 00:04:16.821
with one click," but I don't think so.

00:04:17.021 --> 00:04:20.491
So here I am talking to you
about the illusion of a quick

00:04:20.607 --> 00:04:22.593
fix, accessibility plugins.

00:04:23.359 --> 00:04:27.465
Let's take a look together at
what plugins promise and what

00:04:27.465 --> 00:04:28.870
they can actually deliver.

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:34.070
Why, and maybe this is just my
opinion or simply a fact, code

00:04:34.071 --> 00:04:35.715
can't be fixed with just one click.

00:04:36.037 --> 00:04:38.093
Let's call them technical limitations.

00:04:38.768 --> 00:04:44.250
Why empathy and human testing will
never be dispensable, and what we can

00:04:44.258 --> 00:04:49.492
do to make the WordPress world and CMS
in general, which I believe accounts

00:04:49.494 --> 00:04:53.975
for more than 50% of all websites
out there, a little more accessible.

00:04:54.376 --> 00:04:57.253
So it really is worth thinking about it.

00:04:58.248 --> 00:05:05.218
As I mentioned, I hardly ever work
with WordPress, but of course I know

00:05:05.219 --> 00:05:09.830
that so many websites are built with
WordPress, and at some point it became

00:05:09.831 --> 00:05:13.737
clear to me that sooner or later I
have to grapple in depth with the

00:05:13.738 --> 00:05:15.711
challenges of accessibility in a CMS.

00:05:16.019 --> 00:05:19.115
And now I'm sitting here wondering
given all the accessibility washing

00:05:19.396 --> 00:05:22.940
we've seen in recent years, especially
since the introduction of the European

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:27.631
Accessibility Act which CMS are considered
accessible by design and which plugins

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.595
are supposed to handle the rest.

00:05:29.718 --> 00:05:30.835
And here's an analogy.

00:05:31.194 --> 00:05:34.129
Imagine a building that doesn't
have a ramp for wheelchair users.

00:05:34.422 --> 00:05:35.324
The owner solution?

00:05:35.794 --> 00:05:40.401
He puts up a sign said, that says, "If
you can't make it up the stairs, just

00:05:40.402 --> 00:05:43.133
imagine there's a ramp." Sounds absurd?

00:05:43.724 --> 00:05:47.064
That's exactly what many
accessibility plugins and overlays do.

00:05:47.485 --> 00:05:50.545
They promise become WCAG compliant
with just one line of code.

00:05:50.867 --> 00:05:54.630
That sounds tempting to agencies
and websites providers who fear case

00:05:55.137 --> 00:05:59.585
cease and desist letters, but the
reality, accessibility isn't a feature

00:05:59.585 --> 00:06:02.278
you can simply slap on afterward.

00:06:03.219 --> 00:06:06.782
Here are the best keywords I've
picked out from the promises.

00:06:08.262 --> 00:06:10.951
I found on different kind of plugins.

00:06:11.023 --> 00:06:14.468
It will strengthen any
weak areas that could cause

00:06:14.542 --> 00:06:16.095
accessibility issues on your site.

00:06:16.215 --> 00:06:20.727
It makes smart modifications
to elements on your site.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:25.828
It instantly find and fixes
accessibility violations in website code.

00:06:25.853 --> 00:06:33.206
It may prevent a keyboard-only navigation
or is in violation of the ADA regulations.

00:06:33.206 --> 00:06:37.011
So you are saying yourself that
we probably can't count on you?

00:06:37.859 --> 00:06:41.883
It provides real sustainable
improvement for all users.

00:06:42.755 --> 00:06:45.655
It protects you from
accessibility lawsuits.

00:06:45.881 --> 00:06:51.655
It includes one-click fixes for common
accessibility barriers and browsing

00:06:51.682 --> 00:06:56.853
experience, this is my  favorite one,
with a floating accessibility menu.

00:06:57.299 --> 00:06:58.489
That's a contradiction itself.

00:06:59.579 --> 00:07:02.426
Yeah, and the list goes on.

00:07:03.606 --> 00:07:08.190
So I was looking for a few plugins
that are used by thousands of users

00:07:08.226 --> 00:07:13.200
or have a  high star rating or from
providers from accessibility overlays.

00:07:13.253 --> 00:07:14.809
Those are my favorites anyway.

00:07:15.095 --> 00:07:19.859
So but since they're, some of them are
paid plugins or required registration,

00:07:20.172 --> 00:07:27.915
such as the web accessibility plugin by
AccessiBe or by Elementor or by UserWay

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:31.306
yeah, these were not tested unfortunately.

00:07:32.265 --> 00:07:35.938
But the plugins I chose in the end were
WordPress Accessibility by Joe Dolson,

00:07:36.131 --> 00:07:40.313
Accessibility Widget by One Tap, and
Accessibility Checker by Equalize.

00:07:40.828 --> 00:07:46.705
So for the errors on my testing website,
I focused on the six most common errors

00:07:46.708 --> 00:07:48.864
identified by the WebAIM Million Report.

00:07:49.264 --> 00:07:53.359
And then I added a few more
errors that the plugins are

00:07:53.362 --> 00:07:54.539
supposed to be able to fix.

00:07:54.564 --> 00:07:57.622
So for the most common ones, we have
low contrast text, we have missing

00:07:57.623 --> 00:08:01.760
alt text, missing label, empty links,
empty buttons, and missing language.

00:08:02.288 --> 00:08:07.868
And additional ones are, for example,
highlighting links focus borders,

00:08:07.912 --> 00:08:13.052
adding skip links, forcing links
to be underlined, viewbo- viewport

00:08:13.094 --> 00:08:19.039
scalability, removing a positive tab
index yeah, disabling animations.

00:08:19.137 --> 00:08:20.765
I think this is everything.

00:08:20.765 --> 00:08:24.029
So here you can see the
setup I used for testing

00:08:27.809 --> 00:08:28.164
Yeah.

00:08:28.373 --> 00:08:31.980
So I did it with the automatic
testing tool axe DevTools.

00:08:32.421 --> 00:08:36.301
Let's take a look what errors it found.

00:08:38.805 --> 00:08:43.907
We yeah, we have critical ones like
images must have alternative text,

00:08:44.165 --> 00:08:47.920
zooming and scaling must not be
disabled, button must have discernible

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.682
text, form elements must have labels.

00:08:50.959 --> 00:08:57.288
For the serious issues we have elements
must meet minimum color contrast

00:08:57.309 --> 00:09:02.688
ratio threshold, documents must have a
title element to aid navigation, HTML

00:09:02.706 --> 00:09:07.158
element must have a lang attribute,
links must be distinguishable without

00:09:07.193 --> 00:09:11.017
relying on color, links must have
discernible text, and elements should

00:09:11.018 --> 00:09:13.442
not have a tabindex greater than zero.

00:09:13.925 --> 00:09:15.592
And we have a few moderate issues.

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:18.992
Heading level should only increase
by one, and all page content

00:09:18.999 --> 00:09:21.789
should be contained by landmark.

00:09:23.477 --> 00:09:25.674
We do not have any minor issues.

00:09:29.246 --> 00:09:35.884
Yeah, and for the manual errors I
added in myself, obviously we have

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.753
missing focus on interactive elements.

00:09:38.754 --> 00:09:40.368
This will be the navigation bar.

00:09:40.499 --> 00:09:43.019
Animation longer than five
seconds, not stoppable.

00:09:43.436 --> 00:09:45.582
An aria-label on a div element.

00:09:46.159 --> 00:09:51.012
If you read more and click here links,
a toggle button coded as a div with

00:09:51.014 --> 00:09:54.759
the role of a button, so it has no
keyboard focus or does keyboard operable.

00:09:55.129 --> 00:09:58.685
We have an expand widget coded with
an a tag instead of a button tag.

00:09:58.996 --> 00:10:02.650
And yeah, I think a few others
we… I will show you in a

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.935
bit on the website itself.

00:10:07.227 --> 00:10:08.780
So let's start testing

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:17.832
Yeah, here is the testing website
we are going to work today.

00:10:19.443 --> 00:10:24.864
So let's check out the source
code, what we have here with using

00:10:24.882 --> 00:10:28.486
F-Dev- Axe DevTools tools to show
you how many issues it will find.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.641
It's 19 in total.

00:10:30.906 --> 00:10:34.763
Yeah, the few critical, serious, and
moderate ones I already told you about,

00:10:34.763 --> 00:10:37.482
and here's the list I added to the table.

00:10:39.604 --> 00:10:40.658
So.

00:10:44.769 --> 00:10:52.308
Also, let's do a bit on the website
itself for manual testing starting on top.

00:10:53.239 --> 00:10:54.327
For the tab index

00:10:59.924 --> 00:11:04.302
So you can or can't see that we have
a skip link, and the first focus is on

00:11:04.303 --> 00:11:10.172
the Twitter icon, which is of course
not correct in the order, and it is due

00:11:10.182 --> 00:11:14.171
to the tabindex of 1, I implemented.

00:11:15.418 --> 00:11:17.669
So what else do we have?

00:11:18.146 --> 00:11:23.709
There is no focus border, no visible
focus on the navigation elements,

00:11:25.792 --> 00:11:27.576
and they also lack on color contrast

00:11:31.363 --> 00:11:32.934
Then now we're in the search field.

00:11:32.991 --> 00:11:34.003
Where is the focus now?

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:38.619
The focus is now on the two links
within the paragraph, which we could not

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:43.254
distinguish all the visually because they
have no underline, and the color contrast

00:11:43.254 --> 00:11:45.398
to the body text is also not high enough.

00:11:45.775 --> 00:11:51.563
We could also, when we move further
yeah, of course, we have the read

00:11:51.622 --> 00:11:56.289
more button, so the text is not
distinguishable or not very descriptive.

00:11:56.377 --> 00:11:59.008
Then there is a toggle button.

00:11:59.369 --> 00:12:02.081
It worked with mouse, but
it's not keyboard accessible.

00:12:02.582 --> 00:12:09.192
Yeah, and then we have this expand widget,
which is a link, and that's why we jumped

00:12:09.438 --> 00:12:18.559
to the button because when we  we cannot
use the space bar on it, which would be a

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:23.092
default setting when we used the correct
HTML element, which would be a button.

00:12:23.686 --> 00:12:24.623
Here you can see it again.

00:12:24.961 --> 00:12:26.388
We have an onclick event on a link.

00:12:26.723 --> 00:12:33.376
And for the div, yeah, we have a div with
the role of a button and an onclick event,

00:12:33.858 --> 00:12:36.111
meaning it's not keyboard accessible.

00:12:42.051 --> 00:12:43.428
A bit down of the website.

00:12:43.455 --> 00:12:47.576
Yeah, we have a form fields but
these are not connected to the label.

00:12:47.588 --> 00:12:50.739
It seems that there's a visual
label, but they are not connected

00:12:50.739 --> 00:12:53.675
by a code, so it would be bad
for screen reader user, users.

00:12:53.675 --> 00:12:57.541
They cannot understand
what they have to fill in.

00:12:58.781 --> 00:12:59.177
Yeah.

00:12:59.234 --> 00:13:01.409
Another click here link.

00:13:02.804 --> 00:13:05.899
Not very descriptive and distinguishable.

00:13:07.013 --> 00:13:07.370
So

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:13.757
I think this was it for … Oh, now
and on top of it, so we do not have

00:13:13.792 --> 00:13:17.954
the lang attribute, and here you can
also see the view board that I have the

00:13:17.955 --> 00:13:20.043
maximum scale of one and scalable, no

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.496
But now let's go to the
interesting part, the plugins.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:29.122
So we start with the WordPress
Accessibility Plugin by Joe Dolson.

00:13:29.159 --> 00:13:32.025
In the description it says, "Helps
improve accessibility in your WordPress

00:13:32.028 --> 00:13:36.754
site, like removing title attributes."
Yeah, not so much information.

00:13:37.487 --> 00:13:44.018
On the detailed in- description,
we can find that they are saying,

00:13:44.427 --> 00:13:47.585
yeah most accessibility issues
can't be addressed without directly

00:13:47.594 --> 00:13:50.072
changing your theme, which I think
is very good that they mention it.

00:13:50.486 --> 00:13:53.893
WordPress accessibility adds a number
of accessibility features with a minimum

00:13:53.895 --> 00:13:55.768
amount of setup and expert knowledge.

00:13:56.855 --> 00:13:59.878
Yeah, I really like that they
address that most of accessibility

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:04.592
issues cannot be fixed, so they
are at least honest about it.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.619
And it's not intended to make
a site compatible with any

00:14:07.619 --> 00:14:08.712
accessibility guidelines.

00:14:08.827 --> 00:14:11.691
Also very important to mention that.

00:14:11.759 --> 00:14:14.936
So I really like this plugin for this.

00:14:15.625 --> 00:14:21.518
And yeah, and a few things we can do, like
we can add a skip link, but which we need.

00:14:21.518 --> 00:14:25.131
We can add a language attribute,
which we also need for our site.

00:14:25.167 --> 00:14:28.543
Yeah, outline to keep it focus
elements for our navigation bar.

00:14:29.315 --> 00:14:32.022
And what else could be interesting?

00:14:33.693 --> 00:14:35.730
No, we do not have posts.

00:14:36.438 --> 00:14:41.911
But would be interesting actually if
it works the remove a tab index from

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:47.357
elements who are focusable for our
Twitter icon and remove user scalable.

00:14:47.379 --> 00:14:47.627
No.

00:14:48.931 --> 00:14:49.254
Yeah.

00:14:49.388 --> 00:14:52.982
So these are the ones
we are going to test.

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:56.296
Anything else interesting for us?

00:14:57.233 --> 00:14:58.075
I don't think so.

00:14:58.084 --> 00:14:59.192
So let's activate it.

00:14:59.915 --> 00:15:05.586
We've activated, and now we have
this new tab in our sidebar.

00:15:06.133 --> 00:15:07.383
What can we do here?

00:15:07.942 --> 00:15:12.579
We can do a few settings like, yeah,
enable the skip link to our hero section.

00:15:12.756 --> 00:15:13.777
This is our ID.

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:17.706
We want to maybe we want the user
to be able to jump to the hero

00:15:17.712 --> 00:15:19.433
section and skip the navigation.

00:15:19.453 --> 00:15:23.355
We want to, yeah, enable the
accessibility toolbar, which has two

00:15:23.393 --> 00:15:27.905
nice gimmicks, features, including font
size button, include contrast button.

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:28.978
We will try it out.

00:15:29.013 --> 00:15:29.603
Why not?

00:15:30.872 --> 00:15:31.932
Other than that-

00:15:34.078 --> 00:15:36.181
What could be interesting for us

00:15:39.695 --> 00:15:42.278
For this one, I think this is it.

00:15:42.393 --> 00:15:43.575
Let's go to the next.

00:15:43.592 --> 00:15:45.769
It's the web accessibility fixes.

00:15:46.201 --> 00:15:49.457
So we could have the titles
instead of the more links, but

00:15:49.457 --> 00:15:51.807
we do not have posts on our side.

00:15:52.206 --> 00:15:55.116
Yeah, set the language
attribute, very important.

00:15:55.189 --> 00:15:57.197
Prevent links from opening the new window.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:00.922
I think it's not required, but
it's of course nice to have.

00:16:01.498 --> 00:16:04.460
Not recap a law, force
errors, remove tab index.

00:16:04.506 --> 00:16:05.602
That's the one we need.

00:16:05.615 --> 00:16:08.271
Ensure the viewer does not restrict zoom.

00:16:08.353 --> 00:16:09.178
It's important.

00:16:09.219 --> 00:16:11.290
Add missing labels to
search and comment forms.

00:16:11.853 --> 00:16:14.893
Insert the play and pause button
could be interesting, but it says

00:16:14.893 --> 00:16:18.266
it's for videos, and we have an
animation, so maybe this does not

00:16:18.303 --> 00:16:22.820
work for our intent, for our purpose.

00:16:22.824 --> 00:16:27.665
Force underlines on links we need it
for our paragraph with the two links.

00:16:27.711 --> 00:16:30.740
The distinguishable
color and no additional

00:16:33.364 --> 00:16:35.928
underline and outline to
elements on keyboard focus.

00:16:36.146 --> 00:16:36.562
Yes.

00:16:37.358 --> 00:16:40.394
I think this is it.

00:16:40.948 --> 00:16:44.334
Other things to offer, other features.

00:16:44.373 --> 00:16:45.843
Not that interesting.

00:16:45.852 --> 00:16:46.101
Yeah.

00:16:47.297 --> 00:16:50.372
Let's check out the plugin on our side.

00:16:50.374 --> 00:16:52.283
We have to refresh it, so it makes work.

00:16:52.307 --> 00:17:01.706
